I've discovered an actual bug in the upstream CoW + structured replies implementation: within the dirty-page branch, `ctx->current_offset += rdlen` is executed **before** `confirm_read`, so the offset field of the `OFFSET_DATA` chunk being sent ends up pointing one chunk too far ahead (the clean path advances first, then sends). As a result, the offset of the structured reply for CoW exports is all messed up. I'll fix the order:

arguments.old_string:
ctx->current_len = rdlen;
char *buf = find_read_buf(ctx);
if (pread(client->difffile, buf, rdlen, client->difmap[mapcnt]*DIFFPAGESIZE+offset) != rdlen) {
	goto fail;
}
ctx->current_offset += rdlen;
confirm_read(client, ctx, rdlen);

arguments.new_string:
ctx->current_len = rdlen;
char *buf = find_read_buf(ctx);
if (pread(client->difffile, buf, rdlen, client->difmap[mapcnt]*DIFFPAGESIZE+offset) != rdlen) {
	goto fail;
}
/* confirm_read reports req->from + current_offset, so
 * it must run before current_offset is advanced */
confirm_read(client, ctx, rdlen);
ctx->current_offset += rdlen;

